    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d146">

                <pb facs="0290" n="260" xml:id="pg260"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 7.</note>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">(Extract.)</note>
                <head>Mr. Bancroft to Mr. Fish.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 308.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1871-12-15"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 15, 1871</date>. (Received Jan. 3.)</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>Admiral Prevost, formerly British commissioner for running the northwestern
                    boundary, arrived here this morning and delivered the British Case and evidence,
                    of which I am promised a copy this evening. I will lose no time in sending you a
                    copy and reporting to you the aspect of the case.<seg type="margin">British Case
                        and evidence delivered.</seg></p>
                <p>I remain, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEO. BANCROFT.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
